    <Investigation>
        <name>OSIRIS-APEX Mission</name>
        <type>Mission</type>
        <start_date>2023-09-25</start_date>
        <stop_date xsi:nil="true" nilReason="unknown"/>
        <description>
            The OSIRIS-APEX mission is an extended mission of the OSIRiS-REx mission. APEX uses the capable 
            OSIRIS-REX spacecraft with its complete instrument suite. APEX will distantly observe Apophis during the
            2029 Earth encounter and capture its evolution in real time, revealing the consequences of an asteroid
            undergoing tidal disturbance by a major planet. Beginning in 2029 June, the spacecraft’s instrument suite
            will begin providing high resolution data of this “stony” asteroid — advancing knowledge of these objects
            and their connection to meteorites.
        </description>
